{
  "name": "POC3 — Durable nightly integrity sweep (Release 1)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "cronExpression",
              "expression": "0 3 * * *"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "nightly-schedule",
      "name": "Nightly Schedule",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        300
      ],
      "notes": "The provider HOSTS the schedule; the AI OS journal OWNS the spec.",
      "notesInFlow": false
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "url": "={{ $env.AIOS_WRAPPER_BASE }}/poc3/run-started",
        "method": "POST",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({schedule_id:'poc3-nightly', occurrence: $now.toISO(), provider_correlation_id: $execution.id}) }}",
        "sendHeaders": true,
        "specifyHeaders": "keypair",
        "headerParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "X-Provider-Key",
              "value": "={{ $env.AIOS_PROVIDER_KEY }}"
            },
            {
              "name": "Content-Type",
              "value": "application/json"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {
          "response": {
            "response": {
              "neverError": true,
              "fullResponse": true
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "id": "announce-run-start",
      "name": "Announce Run Start",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        220,
        300
      ],
      "notes": "DECLARATION. Run identity is STUB-MINTED: the run_id comes back from the wrapper and this workflow never chooses one. `provider_correlation_id` is carried separately, explicitly provider-marked, and anchors nothing. 25_ §B: a duplicate declaration of the same (schedule_id, occurrence) is a 409 that PRESERVES the prior started_at and checkpoint count — a duplicate run-started is itself a POC-3 measurement, never an overwrite. An induced mid-flight kill and re-run is expected to produce exactly that 409, and the response carries the prior run_id so this workflow can continue against the original run.",
      "notesInFlow": false
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "url": "={{ $json.stage_endpoint }}",
        "method": "POST",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({run_id: $json.run_id}) }}",
        "options": {
          "retry": {
            "retry": {
              "maxTries": 3,
              "waitBetweenTries": 5000
            }
          },
          "timeout": 30000
        },
        "sendHeaders": true,
        "specifyHeaders": "keypair",
        "headerParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "X-Provider-Key",
              "value": "={{ $env.AIOS_PROVIDER_KEY }}"
            },
            {
              "name": "Content-Type",
              "value": "application/json"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "integrity-sweep-stage",
      "name": "Integrity Sweep Stage",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        440,
        300
      ],
      "notes": "EXECUTION. /stage/deliver is RETRY-TOLERANT by design (25_ §B): the round induces a mid-flight kill, and a single-use rule here would mis-score the provider retry POC-3 exists to measure. Each attempt is counted and recorded.",
      "notesInFlow": false
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "url": "={{ $env.AIOS_WRAPPER_BASE }}/poc3/checkpoint",
        "method": "POST",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({run_id: $('Announce Run Start').item.json.run_id, stage:1}) }}",
        "sendHeaders": true,
        "specifyHeaders": "keypair",
        "headerParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "X-Provider-Key",
              "value": "={{ $env.AIOS_PROVIDER_KEY }}"
            },
            {
              "name": "Content-Type",
              "value": "application/json"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "checkpoint",
      "name": "Checkpoint",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        660,
        300
      ],
      "notes": "Checkpoint state lives in the AI OS ledger — the provider never becomes authoritative for project truth (09_ §2).",
      "notesInFlow": false
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "boolean": [
            {
              "value1": "={{ $json.side_effect_certain }}",
              "value2": true
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "side-effect-certain?",
      "name": "Side Effect Certain?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        880,
        300
      ],
      "notes": "ACT-01. Uncertain outcomes reconcile rather than re-fire.",
      "notesInFlow": false
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "url": "={{ $env.AIOS_WRAPPER_BASE }}/poc3/reconcile",
        "method": "POST",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({run_id: $('Announce Run Start').item.json.run_id}) }}",
        "sendHeaders": true,
        "specifyHeaders": "keypair",
        "headerParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "X-Provider-Key",
              "value": "={{ $env.AIOS_PROVIDER_KEY }}"
            },
            {
              "name": "Content-Type",
              "value": "application/json"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "reconcile",
      "name": "Reconcile",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1100,
        420
      ],
      "notes": "RECONCILIATION. The wrapper compares only what it actually recorded and reports external_post_state_checked: false. It never asserts a check it did not perform, so this workflow must not read the response as certainty about the external side effect.",
      "notesInFlow": false
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "url": "={{ $env.AIOS_WRAPPER_BASE }}/poc3/receipt",
        "method": "POST",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({run_id: $('Announce Run Start').item.json.run_id, occurrence: $('Announce Run Start').item.json.occurrence, provider_status: $json.side_effect_certainty ? 'uncertain' : 'ok'}) }}",
        "sendHeaders": true,
        "specifyHeaders": "keypair",
        "headerParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "X-Provider-Key",
              "value": "={{ $env.AIOS_PROVIDER_KEY }}"
            },
            {
              "name": "Content-Type",
              "value": "application/json"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "report-drift-and-receipt",
      "name": "Report Drift and Receipt",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1320,
        300
      ],
      "notes": "EVIDENCE. 25_ §B lists this route's fields as run_id, occurrence and provider_status in {ok, error, uncertain}; anything else becomes a descriptor under the provider provenance key. The wrapper records, it does not attest — the occurrence window is judged by the real wrapper, not here.",
      "notesInFlow": false
    }
  ],
  "connections": {
    "Nightly Schedule": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Announce Run Start",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "Announce Run Start": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Integrity Sweep Stage",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "Integrity Sweep Stage": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Checkpoint",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "Checkpoint": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Side Effect Certain?",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "Side Effect Certain?": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Report Drift and Receipt",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "node": "Reconcile",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "Reconcile": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Report Drift and Receipt",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    }
  },
  "settings": {
    "executionOrder": "v1"
  },
  "pinData": {},
  "meta": {
    "poc": "POC-3",
    "scenario": "Durable nightly integrity sweep (09_ §2)",
    "partition": "business",
    "task": "TASK-0007",
    "status": "NOT TESTED",
    "contract": "25_ Revision 5 (§A/§B)"
  }
}
